Hi Marya Aldecoa,

This is a bit of a crude way to do it, but I often just read another tsv file with rsID and SNP data and merge with the GWAS summary statistic.

Following are variants from 1000 Genomes, processed by developers of GWASLab <https://github.com/Cloufield/gwaslab>:

hg19: https://www.dropbox.com/s/37p2u1xwmux4gwo/1kg_dbsnp151_hg19_auto.txt.gz?dl=1
hg38: https://www.dropbox.com/s/ouf60n7gdz6cm0g/1kg_dbsnp151_hg38_auto.txt.gz?dl=1

This should cover 99% of the variants, including the HapMap 3 variants for LDSC.

Regards,
Jeff

